---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How does this actually help with vibe coding?",
    a: `When you're building with Claude, Cursor, or ChatGPT, you're constantly explaining what you see on screen. "The button in the top right is misaligned," "the color is wrong on hover," "the spacing between these two elements looks off."

With Nudgy, you skip all of that. Capture your screen, circle the problem, drop the screenshot into your AI. It sees exactly what you see. No guessing, no back-and-forth.

Vibe coding is about staying in flow. Nudgy keeps you there.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Which AI tools does this work with?",
    a: `Every major AI tool that accepts images. Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, and Cursor all handle annotated screenshots natively. Just paste or attach and go.

It also works with CLI tools like Claude Code in Terminal, which reads images directly. And any AI-powered IDE, agent, or assistant that supports image input.

If your AI tool can see images, Nudgy works with it.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Does an annotated screenshot actually produce better AI responses?",
    a: `Significantly. AI models are multimodal — they understand images natively. An annotated screenshot with an arrow pointing at a bug gives the model far more context than a paragraph of text trying to describe it.

Think of it this way: you wouldn't describe a painting to someone standing next to you. You'd point at it. Same principle.

Less ambiguity in, better output out.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Why not just use the built-in macOS screenshot tool?",
    a: `macOS captures great screenshots. But the moment you need to circle something, draw an arrow, or write "fix this" next to a bug, you're opening Preview or another app and losing your flow.

Nudgy does capture and annotation in one step. Shortcut, select, annotate, copy. You're back in your AI tool in seconds, not minutes.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Does anything get uploaded or sent to a server?",
    a: `No. Nudgy runs entirely on your Mac. No cloud, no server, no analytics, no telemetry. Your screenshots never leave your machine unless you explicitly choose to share them.

This matters especially if you're working on proprietary code, internal tools, or client projects. Your visual context stays private.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How fast is the workflow?",
    a: `Under 10 seconds from shortcut to annotated screenshot in your AI tool. And that's if you're taking your time.

The global shortcut triggers from anywhere, so you never leave the app you're working in. Capture, mark up, paste. That's the whole flow.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Who is Nudgy for?",
    a: `Anyone building with AI who communicates visually. Vibe coders, frontend developers, designers, product managers, QA engineers.

If you've ever spent three paragraphs trying to describe a UI bug that you could have just circled, Nudgy is for you. If you paste screenshots into Claude or Cursor as part of your workflow, Nudgy makes that workflow dramatically faster.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Is it really free?",
    a: `The core product is free forever. Capture, annotate, save locally — no limits on that for 25 screenshots per month, no account required.

Pro tiers unlock unlimited screenshots, shareable links, animated GIFs, and cloud storage for teams that need more. But the free version is a fully capable tool, not a trial.`,
  },
];
---

<section class="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="heading">FAQ</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="list">
      {faqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="item">
          <summary class="question">
            <span>{item.q}</span>
            <svg class="chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <div class="answer-inner">
              {item.a.split('\n\n').map((para) => (
                <p>{para}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('details.item').forEach(details => {
    const summary = details.querySelector('summary')!;
    const answer = details.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.answer')!;

    summary.addEventListener('click', e => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (details.open) {
        answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + 'px';
        requestAnimationFrame(() => { answer.style.maxHeight = '0'; });
        answer.addEventListener('transitionend', () => { details.open = false; }, { once: true });
      } else {
        details.open = true;
        answer.style.maxHeight = '0';
        requestAnimationFrame(() => { answer.style.maxHeight = answer.scrollHeight + 'px'; });
        answer.addEventListener('transitionend', () => { answer.style.maxHeight = ''; }, { once: true });
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .faq {
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem 6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .container {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .section-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.12;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .item {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .question {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 0;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .question::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  .question:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .chevron {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: transform 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .item[open] .chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .item[open] .question {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .answer {
    overflow: hidden;
    max-height: 0;
    transition: max-height 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .item[open] .answer {
    max-height: 600px;
  }

  .answer-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .answer p {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
</style>
